{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>For a hand.</b> Like \"for I lift my hand to heaven\" (Deuteronomy 32:40), and the meaning is that HaShem placed His hand upon His throne, and this is an oath. And Rabbi Yeshuah said: a strong hand will be for the one who sits first on the throne of Israel, as is said of Solomon, \"on the throne of YHWH\" (1 Chronicles 29:23), and the meaning concerns Saul."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:22.576976235Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}